## Current Harbor Structure

Default current layout:

```text
<task-id>/
├── task/
│   ├── task.toml
│   ├── instruction.md
│   ├── environment/
│   │   ├── Dockerfile
│   │   ├── repo/
│   │   └── problem_statement.md
│   ├── solution/
│   │   ├── solve.sh
│   │   └── golden.patch
│   └── tests/
│       ├── test.sh
│       ├── tests.patch
│       ├── config.json
│       └── grade.py
└── runs/
```

### Component explanations

| Component | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `task.toml` | Metadata, timeouts, resources, source, category, difficulty explanation |
| `instruction.md` | Problem statement and measurable success criteria given to the agent |
| `environment/Dockerfile` | Container build (base image + setup) |
| `environment/repo/` | Cloned base repository the agent and verifier run against |
| `environment/problem_statement.md` | Must be an **exact copy** of `instruction.md` |
| `solution/solve.sh` | Oracle script that applies or produces the solved state |
| `solution/golden.patch` | Canonical self-contained solution patch (all solution changes) |
| `tests/test.sh` | Runs the suite and writes reward (e.g. `/logs/verifier/reward.txt`) |
| `tests/tests.patch` | Contains fail-to-pass test additions applied at verify time |
| `tests/config.json` | How to run the suite; which test ids are fail-to-pass / pass-to-pass |
| `tests/grade.py` | Grading script |
| `runs/` | Top-level agent execution logs, episodes, and outcomes (reference only; not uploaded) |

If a downloaded task contains `solution/solution.patch` instead of `golden.patch`, rename it to `golden.patch`.

