## Agent-Run Analysis

Preserve these useful older practices (still current):

- Inspect **all** failing agent trials rather than one convenient trial.
- Inspect at least one passing trial when available.
- Use run logs to identify timeout patterns, systematic misunderstandings, and instability.
- Cite concrete observations when they support a verdict or timeout/metadata tweak.

### Historical note on run counts

Some older packages have several trials per model. Newer batches may contain fewer (for example, batches from April 28 2026 onward often include two runs — one per model). A smaller set for newer batches is expected and is **not** automatically a packaging defect.

